The founder's ruling of 2026-11-04 (live, 21:43Z, relayed by the Viola overseer, snapshot `.andromeda/runs/2026-11-04T23-11-43-wrap/inputs/I2-restructure-linux-only.md.txt` items 4 and 5): Viola's target is Linux alone until it works well there, the Windows and macOS code removed behind the tag `multi-os-final` at the route entry "Linux-only code and CI". A capability with an OS clause keeps its Linux half; this one is re-worded to it, nothing deferred (the overseer's technical answer at this wrap's dialog, founder-delegated, 2026-11-05 06:00Z, recorded in `.andromeda/runs/2026-11-04T23-11-43-wrap/adaptation-record.md`). The ground is the founder's own ruling; only the choice to re-word rather than defer, and the card approving this text (2026-11-05 06:03Z), are the overseer's delegate answers.
— was: title «Three-OS CI pipeline from the first commit» · requirement «every push and PR runs build, format, lint (warnings fatal), the tokio-free check of the sync crates, the dependency policy (licences, C-crate, tokio and banned-crate rules, advisories, sources), workflow linting and tests, natively on Windows, macOS and Linux; all actions are SHA-pinned under least-privilege permissions; a weekly scheduled advisory check runs without code changes; the perf gates run in their own job; tools the gates need are checked present first and fail loudly if missing; test homes survive until every gate has read them; and nothing from a test home is uploaded unless the secret scan passed.» · acceptance «Every push and pull request produces a pipeline run on Windows, macOS and Linux covering build, formatting, fatal lint, the tokio-free check of the sync crates, the dependency policy, workflow linting and tests; a weekly scheduled advisory run executes without code changes; the perf gates run in a job of their own; a missing gate tool fails the run loudly; test homes survive until every gate has read them; and nothing from a test home is uploaded from a run whose secret scan failed.»

2026-11-05 (2026-11-05-linux-only-code-and-ci, phase P5): not claimed. This chunk makes CI Linux-only: `ci.yml`'s four matrix jobs keep `ubuntu-latest` alone, the Windows steps and `windows-mutants.yml` go. The acceptance's outcome, a pipeline run on every push, is read only by the operator pass's CI read, never at an implement-time ref. Its dependency-policy clause (advisories) reads red on RUSTSEC-2026-0441 (`pin-utils` via `portable-pty =0.8.1` → `nix 0.25.1`), which a CARRY on «Version done-check» owns (`inputs#I3`). On the operator's word at P5 (`inputs#I4`, card `.andromeda/runs/2026-11-05T08-59-20-phase/p5-card-1.md`), the cap's owner is «Version done-check», provable at its CI read once the CARRY's remedy lands.
